cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "EconomicsPro: a browser-based platform for the economic and financial appraisal of agrifood projects"
abstract: >-
  EconomicsPro is a self-contained web application that carries an agricultural or agro-industrial project
  through a whole appraisal in the browser, with no installation and no server-side computation. It defines the
  project and its assumptions (horizon, constant or current prices, discount rate by MARR, WACC or CAPM, tax
  regime with the exemption of article 74 of the Mexican income tax law), deflates and projects the price and
  yield series by five methods, builds the sales programme, the investment schedule with automatic replacement,
  the operating budget and the working capital, arranges the loans and the pro-forma statements with the two
  cash flows, and appraises them with net present value, all the roots of the internal rate of return, modified
  IRR, benefit-cost ratio, payback and equivalent annual value, together with the partial budgets and marginal
  analysis of the CIMMYT manual. It then submits the result to risk (switching values, tornado, scenarios and a
  Monte Carlo simulation with rank correlation), converts it to economic prices with conversion factors and an
  exact bridge from the private to the economic NPV, compares alternatives (incremental IRR, capital rationing,
  economic life, Faustmann rotation, buy or lease), and exports the figures, a self-contained report and a
  package that lets anyone redo every calculation. Every method is cited to its source.
type: software
